NODE RETENTION REFERENCE
========================
Quick reference: for each C++ node type that survives in the final AST,
what does it represent and what are its children (left to right).

The one rule to remember: when a passAlong action fires (e.g. #class, #impl),
it pops the top node, copies its data into a NEW C++ type, and deletes the old one.
The C++ type changes; the semanticMeaning field stays the same.
Visitor dispatch is based on C++ type, so use the SURVIVING type in your visit().

HOW KEYWORD LEAVES DISAPPEAR (makeBinarySubTreeWithHead):
  write/read/return/if/while statements all use makeBinarySubTreeWithHead(count).
  It pops `count` nodes and restores them in push order. The FIRST one (the keyword
  leaf) is promoted into the new node via copyNode — its semanticMeaning is absorbed.
  The keyword leaf does NOT survive as a child. Only the remaining nodes do.

HOW ASSIGNMENT CHILDREN ARE ORDERED (makeBinarySubTree mode 1):
  Pops first=expr(top), second=assign(middle, promoted), third=variable(bottom).
  Result: children[0]=variable(LHS), children[1]=expr(RHS).
  The doc note about "top-of-stack first" was wrong; the code does {third,first}.

HOW DOT CHILDREN ARE ORDERED (makeBinarySubTree mode 0):
  Pops first=top(member/action), second=object.
  Result: children[0]=member/action(RHS), children[1]=object(LHS).


========================================================================
SURVIVING NODE TYPES — what each one IS and what children it has
========================================================================

--- Statements ---

reptstatement4Node   Assignment statement  (e.g.  x := expr ;)
  nodeValue          ":="
  2 children:
  children[0]        reptvariable2andidNode   — LHS variable (id + optional indices)
  children[1]        exprNode                 — RHS value
  NOTE: makeBinarySubTree mode 1 pops expr(top), assign(middle, absorbed), variable(bottom).
  children = {variable, expr} so children[0]=LHS, children[1]=RHS.

freturnstatementNode  Return statement  (e.g.  return ( expr ) ;)
  semanticMeaning    "return"  (absorbed from the return keyword leaf)
  1 child:
  children[0]        exprNode             — returned expression

writestatementNode   Write statement  (e.g.  write ( expr ) ;)
  semanticMeaning    "write"  (absorbed from the write keyword leaf)
  1 child:
  children[0]        exprNode             — expression to write

readstatementNode    Read statement  (e.g.  read ( variable ) ;)
  semanticMeaning    "read"  (absorbed from the read keyword leaf)
  1 child:
  children[0]        reptvariable2andidNode — variable to read into

ifstatementNode      If statement  (e.g.  if (...) then ... else ... ;)
  semanticMeaning    "if"  (absorbed from the if keyword leaf)
  3 children:
  children[0]        conditionNode        — condition (relexpr)
  children[1]        thenNode             — then branch (statblock)
  children[2]        felseNode            — else branch (statblock)

whilestatementNode   While statement  (e.g.  while (...) statblock ;)
  semanticMeaning    "while"  (absorbed from the while keyword leaf)
  2 children:
  children[0]        conditionNode        — condition (relexpr)
  children[1]        statblockNode        — loop body

dotNode              Dot-access chain  (e.g.  a.b  or  self.f().g)
  2 children (object pushed first, member/action pushed second):
  children[0]        member/action node   — RHS: the method call, member access, or
                                            assignment being performed on the object
                                            (aparamsandidNode, reptvariable2andidNode,
                                             or reptstatement4Node)
  children[1]        object node          — LHS: the object being accessed
                                            (selfandidnest2Node or reptvariable2andidNode)

--- Expressions ---

exprNode             Expression (arithExpr optionally followed by a relop + arithExpr)
  1 child (no relop):
    children[0]      arithexprNode
  2 children (with relop — epsilon child is filtered):
    children[0]      expr2Node            — relop + second arithexpr
    children[1]      arithexprNode        — first arithexpr

arithexprNode        Arithmetic expression  (term with optional +/- chain)
  1 child:
  children[0]        termNode             — if no addop chain
                  OR rightrecarithexprNode — if an addop chain was built

rightrecarithexprNode  One node in an addOp chain  (e.g.  + term)
  nodeValue          "+", "-", or "or"
  2 children:
  children[0]        left operand         — arithexprNode or prior rightrecarithexprNode
  children[1]        right operand        — termNode

termNode             Term  (factor with optional */ chain)
  1 child:
  children[0]        factorNode           — if no multop chain
                  OR rightrectermNode     — if a multop chain was built

rightrectermNode     One node in a multOp chain  (e.g.  * factor)
  nodeValue          "*", "/", or "and"
  2 children:
  children[0]        left operand         — termNode or prior rightrectermNode
  children[1]        right operand        — factorNode

factorNode           Factor  (literal, variable, parenthesised expr, function call)
  1 child:
  children[0]        intNode | floatnumNode | reptvariable2andidNode | aparamsandidNode

factor2Node          Negated / signed factor  (e.g.  not f   or   -f)
  2 children:
  children[0]        signNode or 'not' keyword leaf
  children[1]        factorNode

aparamsandidNode     Function call  (id ( args ))
  2 children:
  children[0]        idNode               — function name
  children[1]        aparamsNode          — argument list

reptvariable2andidNode  Variable reference with optional indices  (e.g.  a[i][j])
  2 children:
  children[0]        idNode               — variable name
  children[1]        reptvariable2Node    — index list (epsilon-equivalent if no indices)

aparamsNode          Actual argument list
  0..N children (epsilon-terminated):
  children[0..N-1]   exprNode             — one per argument

indiceNode           One array index  (e.g.  [ expr ])
  1 child:
  children[0]        arithexprNode        — index expression

--- Declarations ---

classNode            Class declaration  (semanticMeaning = "classdecl")
  stEntry.name       class name
  stEntry.type       inherited class names (from isalist)
  stMap              symbol table: member variables + member functions
  3 children (optclassdecl2 is epsilon-equivalent and invisible when no inheritance):
  children[0]        idNode               — class name
  children[1]        optclassdecl2Node    — isalist (not visible in AST if no base classes)
  children[2]        reptclassdecl4Node   — class body ({ member declarations })

funcNode             Free function or main  (semanticMeaning = "funcdef")
  stEntry.name       function name
  stEntry.type       return type
  stMap              symbol table: params + locals
  2 children:
  children[0]        funcheadNode         — function signature (id, params, returntype)
  children[1]        funcbodyNode         — function body (locals + statements)

implNode             Method implementation  (semanticMeaning = "impldef")
  stEntry.name       class name
  stMap              keyed by function name → funcEntry
  2 children:
  children[0]        funcheadNode         — method signature (class id, method id, params, returntype)
  children[1]        reptimpldef3Node     — method body (locals + statements)

funcdeclfamNode      Member function declaration  (visibility + funchead)
  stEntry.name       function name
  stEntry.type       return type
  stEntry.visibility "public" or "private"
  2 children:
  children[0]        visibilityNode       — "public" or "private"
  children[1]        funcdeclNode         — function signature (id, params, returntype)

attributedeclfamNode Member variable declaration  (visibility + vardecl)
  stEntry.name       variable name
  stEntry.type       variable type
  stEntry.visibility "public" or "private"
  2 children:
  children[0]        visibilityNode       — "public" or "private"
  children[1]        attributedeclNode    — variable declaration (id + type)

funcdeclNode         Function signature inside a class
  stEntry.name       function name
  stEntry.type       return type
  stEntry.link       → fparams stMap
  1..3 children (epsilon-terminated; id absent for constructors, returntype absent for constructors):
  children[0]        idNode               — method name  (absent for constructors)
  children[?]        fparamsNode          — parameter list (always present)
  children[?]        returntypeNode       — return type leaf  (absent for constructors)

funcheadNode         Function header (free function or impl method)
  stEntry.name       function name
  stEntry.type       return type
  stEntry.link       → funcparams stMap
  Variable children (epsilon-terminated):
  Free function:     idNode, fparamsNode (if params exist), returntypeNode/voidNode
  Impl method:       idNode(class name), idNode(method name), fparamsNode, returntypeNode/voidNode

funcbodyNode         Function body
  stMap              local variable declarations
  0..N children (epsilon-terminated):
  children[0..N-1]   localvardeclNode and/or statement nodes (in source order)

vardeclNode          Variable declaration  (id : type [dims] ;)
  stEntry.name       variable name
  stEntry.type       variable type
  2–3 children:
  children[0]        idNode               — variable name
  children[1]        typeNode             — variable type
  children[2]        reptvardecl3Node     — dimension list / dimlist (absent if no dimensions)

localvardeclNode     Local variable declaration  (local id : type ;)
  stEntry.name       variable name
  stEntry.type       variable type
  2–3 children:
  children[0]        idNode               — variable name
  children[1]        typeNode             — variable type
  children[2]        reptvardecl3Node     — dimension list / dimlist (absent if no dimensions)

attributedeclNode    Class attribute declaration  (attribute id : type ;)
  stEntry.name       attribute name
  stEntry.type       attribute type
  2 children:
  children[0]        idNode               — attribute name
  children[1]        typeNode             — attribute type

paramNode            Function parameter
  stEntry.name       parameter name
  stEntry.type       parameter type
  2 children (epsilon-terminated):
  children[0]        idNode               — parameter name
  children[1]        typeNode             — parameter type

--- Structural ---

startNode            AST root  (the whole program)
  stMap              global symbol table: class + free function entries
  0..N children (epsilon-terminated):
  children[0..N-1]   classNode, implNode, or funcNode  (in source order)

statblockNode        Block of statements  ({ stmt stmt ... })
  0..N children (epsilon-terminated):
  children[0..N-1]   statement nodes (reptstatement4Node, writestatementNode, etc.)

conditionNode        Condition in if/while  (semanticMeaning = "relexpr")
  NOTE: conditionNode IS the relexpr — it passAlongs from relexprNode and inherits
  its 3 children directly. There is no wrapper relexprNode child.
  3 children:
  children[0]        arithexprNode        — left-hand side of comparison
  children[1]        relopNode            — relational operator (==, <>, <, >, <=, >=)
  children[2]        arithexprNode        — right-hand side of comparison

thenNode             Then-branch of if  (or body of while, semanticMeaning = "reptstatblock1")
  0..N children (epsilon-terminated):
  children[0..N-1]   statement nodes

felseNode            Else-branch of if  (semanticMeaning = "reptstatblock1" or epsilon if absent)
  0..N children (epsilon-terminated; empty when there is no else clause):
  children[0..N-1]   statement nodes

reptimpldef3Node     Body of a method implementation
  0..N children (epsilon-terminated):
  children[0..N-1]   localvardeclNode and/or statement nodes (in source order)

--- Leaves (0 children) ---

idNode              identifier              nodeValue = name
intNode             integer literal         nodeValue = "42"
floatnumNode        float literal           nodeValue = "3.14"
typeNode            type keyword            nodeValue = "int" | "float" | <classname>
addopNode           additive operator       nodeValue = "+" | "-" | "or"
multopNode          multiplicative operator nodeValue = "*" | "/" | "and"
relopNode           relational operator     nodeValue = "==" | "<>" | "<" | ">" | "<=" | ">="
assignNode          assignment operator     nodeValue = ":="  (leaf only; its data is absorbed
                                            into reptstatement4Node by makeBinarySubTree mode 1)
signNode            unary sign              nodeValue = "+" | "-"
visibilityNode      visibility keyword      nodeValue = "public" | "private"
voidNode            void keyword            nodeValue = "void"
selfNode            self keyword
ifNode              if keyword
whileNode           while keyword
readNode            read keyword
writeNode           write keyword
returnNode          return keyword
epsilonNode         stack sentinel — never appears in the final tree


